      "answer": "**Answer:** The externally managed Python environment marker is defined by **PEP 668 — \"Marking Python base environments as 'externally managed'\"** (Status: Final). The authoritative PEP header, fetched and verified verbatim from the official python/peps source, reads: \"PEP: 668 Title: Marking Python base environments as “externally managed”\", and its abstract states: \"This PEP proposes a mechanism for a Python installation to communicate to tools like pip that its global package installation context is managed by some means external to Python, such as an OS package manager.\" The marker itself is the `EXTERNALLY-MANAGED` file specified by this PEP and standardized in the PyPA packaging specification.\n\nSources:\n- \n- \n- \n\nFINAL LABEL: supported\n\nSources:\n- https://discuss.python.org/t/pep-668-marking-python-base-environments-as-externally-managed/10302\n- https://github.com/pypa/packaging.python.org/blob/main/source/specifications/externally-managed-environments.rst\n- https://github.com/python/peps/blob/main/peps/pep-0668.rst\n- https://peps.python.org/pep-0668\n- https://pydevtools.com/handbook/explanation/what-is-pep-668\n- https://raw.githubusercontent.com/python/peps/main/peps/pep-0668.rst",
